      "message": "freezegun is technically considered a third-party library, which we should be able to include in the second stanza of imports (starting at line 20 with fixtures):\n\n  import fixtures\n  import freezegun\n  import mock\n\nLike the examples here [0] we can see the first set of imports is reserved for standard library namespaces, then third-party libraries, and finally imports that are relative to the project (i.e. things within keystone).\n\n[0] http://docs.openstack.org/developer/hacking/#real-world-import-order-examples",
      "revId": "e68dd0a5d86aed977ed0c6a55613cd6697414bfb",
