      "writtenOn": "2016-12-19T20:41:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Huh - interesting. This is what drops the time context all together, right? That\u0027s kind of a neat pattern. This is what I\u0027ve had to do in the past in order to get around weird issues with SQLite + freezegun [0]. Specifically when trying to advance the clock in freezegun by hours or days:\n\n  frozen_datetime.tick(delta\u003ddatetime.timedelta(days\u003d2))\n\nThis isn\u0027t really susceptible to that behavior because you\u0027re not using the context manager within freezegun to advance through large chunks of time. I\u0027ll have to keep this one in my back pocket. Thanks!\n\n[0] https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/c69df5bea9f27a508102b885ce1647e9e5d789ac/keystone/tests/unit/test_v3_auth.py#L299-L302",
